hero some folks definitions welcome to  our when it comes to the collision  between two worlds Capcom Zone versus  fighting game series is arguably the  best in the business it's been over five  years since we last saw Marvel's finest  go toe-to-toe with Capcom's beloved  franchises and now it's time for another  clash with Marvel vs. Capcom infinite so  what's changed what's new what crazy  mechanics has Capcom come up with this  time well keep watching to find out and  if you want more coverage of NBC and all  the latest fighting games don't forget  to subscribe to the GameSpot YouTube  channel because I guarantee you we're  going to have a lot more to talk about  in the future but for right now let's  get into what we know so far based on  the first trailer that we all saw back  in December Infinite will return to a  2v2 format which hasn't been seen since  the first Marvel vs. Capcom nearly  twenty years ago many people in the  Marvel community were hoping for  something just as hype and combo  friendly as MVC 3 woods but we had a  chance to check out the game at Capcom's  offices and by golly it's a different  beast altogether there's a lot to get  through so let's start off with the  basics  first off infinite has thrown the button  layout from MBC three out the window and  has returned to a four button setup  similar to MBC two punches and kicks  both get a light and hard variation but  characteristics a staple and the marvel  of franchises for decades are now gone  instead the final two buttons will be  used for tagging your partner and using  your infinity stone power now tagging a  partner will cause them to run on the  screen and you can immediately begin  attacking with them but what makes this  mechanic special is that you can tag it  anytime anywhere in the middle of an air  combo sure tagging your partner  throw a fireball and then immediately  tag in yeah you can do that activate a  hyper combo and then tag in and rush  them down with high-low mix-ups yes you  can do that too the game may lack this  but it makes up for it by allowing you  to essentially create your own no longer  will characters be thrown aside because  their assists are weak or be essential  to a team all of dr. doom because of  their versatility while this may seem  weird at first after all Marvel players  the world round loved their assist it  all plays into the main mechanic that  drives infinite combo system and if  Capcom statements about making the game  more accessible put you in a panic well  I can assure you that there's nothing to  worry about they have made the game  easier for casuals by introducing an  auto combo system that simply involves  pressing the light punch one mashing the  button won't exactly win you the game  but it's a smart move for people who  don't play religiously to stand a  fighting chance  and speaking of combos they're just as  deep and complex as ever ground balances  and wall bouncers make the return oh and  every single character can ocg by  themselves but there is a huge potential  for creativity when it comes to combos  in this game and we haven't even touched  on the insanity stones yet well actually  let's do that right now so each of the  six Infinity stones grant your character  in infinity search a special power that  you can use at any point during the  match  Capcom shows off three of the stones in  the build that we played the time stone  which gives your character a warp - the  power stone which gives you a  short-range wall bounce attack and the  space stone which allows you to suck  enemies in perfect for command grabs the  stones abilities are decently powered by  themselves but build enough meter and  you'll be able to unleash the infinity  storm effect the powered up time stone  speeds you  significantly throwing any recovery  frames out the window and allowing you  to chain together moves into custom  combos the power stone surge amplifies  our damage and gives every move you  connected with a giant ground or wall  balance but my favorite out of all the  three definitely has to be the space  stone surge which simply enough traps  your opponent in a giant box they can  still attack and block but they're stuck  there for a while just waiting to be  rushed down even by Marvel vs. Capcom  standards these stones are pretty insane  and honestly I don't think I'm going to  miss x-factor all that much oh and one  last thing you can say goodbye to one  player games because now whenever your  character is caught in a combo with  certain deaths on the horizon you can  activate a counter switch and what that  does is call in your second character  who you now control while your opponent  is beating up the first so this opens up  the game's defensive options while also  putting pressure on the attacker to  continue their combo or not it does cost  two super mirrors to activate the camera  switch but I take that over a dead  character any day now there's a lot more  I haven't mentioned and I don't really  want to drag this on too long so I'm  just going to do a rundown everything I  missed ready go rock Iraq who's in the  trailer but not playable on the latest  build so that does give me hope for a  Groot as a character at least the  footage here may not show it but if you  time it right  push blocking will actually reflect  projectile yep finally a counter against  Morgan doom  Ultron might be the only brand-new  character so far but everyone at least  feels slightly different from the  previous Marvel vs. Capcom iterations  and despite being beaten up in every  trailer that we've seen Mega Man  actually looks pretty cool his moveset  has a ton of awesome projectiles and his  ex armor actually powers them up  not unlike Arthur and finally ending  this on a weird little note dead  characters actually stay on the screen  for some reason maybe it's a distraction  or maybe it's an intimidation factor for  the other team I don't know it's kind of  weird it's pretty crazy that were  already less than five months away from  new Marvel vs. Capcom so as we get  closer to the September release we'll  have a lot more information about the  game so please keep it tuned the  GameSpot and subscribe to our YouTube  channel for all the latest of things  Oh  [Music]  [Applause]  [Music]
 

